<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>My Dinh by Motorbike: Motorbike Route Connections in Hanoi</h1>
<p>My Dinh&rsquo;s riding story is a story of connections, because the modern quarter in Nam Tu Liem is a base first and a destination second, linked eastward through the city&rsquo;s middle districts to the historic centre, westward into the wider modern west of Cau Giay and Bac Tu Liem, and across the whole map to the rental counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien on the river&rsquo;s far side. The corridors make these connections the most legible on the near map, and the skill the quarter asks is the planner&rsquo;s one, knowing which line serves which trip and at which hour. This page reads those connections honestly, without fabricated journey times, because duration is the day&rsquo;s own fact and the honest guide teaches the shape.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, and the connection to it is the plan&rsquo;s longest spine. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/my-dinh-rental-planning/">My Dinh rental planning</a> page for the base-first picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/nam-tu-liem-route-connections/">Nam Tu Liem route connections</a> page for the district-level network.</p>
<nav class="toc">
